+	is 20–500; peak is 40–10000; fullFrame is between white and peak. Settings
+	apply only in HDR mode. White adjusts SDR content while retaining absolute
+	PQ levels. The other limits are shared with color-managed applications;
+	they do not constitute a measured color correction. An output entry with
+	enabled="false" restores defaults. Reloads take effect at frame boundaries.
+
+*<colorManagement><output name="..." profile="..." calibration="..." sdrBitDepth="..." />*
+	Configure SDR color management independently for each connector. Later
+	entries take precedence. Changes apply on reconfigure. *profile* is an
+	absolute path to an ICC v2 or v4 RGB display profile (maximum 16 MiB).
+	An empty or omitted path removes the profile. Vulkan is required for ICC
+	conversion. Invalid profiles retain the last successfully applied profile.
+
+	*calibration* accepts true or false (default true). When enabled, the
+	profile's VCGT calibration curves are applied once after color conversion.
+	External gamma controls are suspended while an ICC profile or HDR is active.
+	*sdrBitDepth* accepts 8 (default) or 10. The compositor falls back to 8-bit
